sorry, I forgot the top-post rule.
=E2=80=8B

g_at_chat_send(data->modem, "AT&C0", NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

Was this change required?  I didn't think Telit suffered from dropping carr=
ier issue.  If so, feel free to send a patch.

=E2=80=8BThis change was necessary because the he910 was putting the DCD si=
gnal to low after ppp session, so it was impossible to connect again to tha=
t port.=E2=80=8B
=E2=80=8BSetting &C0 in the modem port forces DCD to stay high.
=E2=80=8B

oFono expects auto-attach to be disabled.  So this change is actually incor=
rect.  What was going wrong that was fixed by this change?

=E2=80=8BRegarding the AUTOATT change, I had to move it to post_online sect=
ion because it was issued too early in modem startup and it always returned=
 an error.
Then I changed it to 1 because there was some misalignment between modem at=
tachment status and ofono variables.
I didn't go to deep in this problem but putting AUTOATT to 1 solved my prob=
lem and is good for me.

